<title>USA: U.S. Treasury balances at Fed fell on May 2.</title>
<headline>U.S. Treasury balances at Fed fell on May 2.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury balances at Federal Reserve based on Treasury Department's latest budget statement.</p>
<p>			  (BILLIONS OF DLRS)</p>
<p>				   May 2		  May 1</p>
<p>Fed acct			21.260		 38.653</p>
<p>Tax/loan note acct	  38.529		 36.553</p>
<p>Cash balance		  59.789		 77.206</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>Total public debt,</p>
<p> subject to limit	5,244.832	     5,251.417</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>Treasury said individual income tax refunds valued at $5.447 billion were issued and $24 million of corporate refunds were issued.</p>
</text>
